    "pt": {
      "status": "llm-draft",
      "generated": "2026-09-22",
      "method": "LLM-generated initial translation in Portuguese with Acordo Ortográfico spelling readable in Brazil and Portugal, using established Portuguese-language print-trade terminology (offset plano/rotativo, rotogravura, flexografia, serigrafia, tipografia, encadernação colada/canoa/espiral, vinco, corte e vinco, papel couché/offset, gramatura, cor especial/Pantone, acabamento, laminação, verniz, substrato). Brand names, format codes and ISO references pass through unchanged, as in the other languages. Translations are kept as reviewable data files in tools/i18n/.",
      "review": "Not yet reviewed by a professional Portuguese-language print-domain translator. Brazil is the natural review channel (largest Portuguese-language print market); a Portuguese (PT) reviewer for European usage is welcome. Candidate for the first language-sponsorship (SD-0017 §3)."
    },
    "hi": {
      "status": "llm-draft",
      "generated": "2026-09-22",
      "method": "LLM-generated initial translation in Hindi (Devanagari script). Follows Indian print-trade practice: established English trade terms are transliterated into Devanagari where that is what the trade says (ऑफसेट, लैमिनेशन, फ्लेक्सो, डाई-कट, कोटेड पेपर, पैंटोन), native Hindi is used where it is current (कागज़, छपाई, बाइंडिंग/जिल्दसाज़ी, मोड़, रंग, आकार). Brand names, format codes and ISO references pass through unchanged. Translations are kept as reviewable data files in tools/i18n/.",
      "review": "Not yet reviewed by a professional Hindi print-domain translator. Reviewer channel to be confirmed (North Indian print associations; Delhi/Mumbai printers). English remains the working language of much of the Indian trade, so Hindi labels serve buyers first."
